# Copy to build.env (not in git) and set what differs on your machine; every line is optional, and a variable already
# set in the environment wins over this file. Read by scripts/deploy.sh, and through bash by mcp_call.py and
# mcp_smoke.py, so shell quoting and # comments mean the same for all three.
# The Windows dotnet.exe, as a WSL path (default: dotnet.exe on PATH). global.json pins the SDK deploy.sh builds with.
# MELE_DOTNET='/mnt/c/Program Files/dotnet/dotnet.exe'
# The Legendary Edition folder, as a Windows path (default: unset, and the server finds the game in the registry).
# MELE_LE_DIR='C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Mass Effect Legendary Edition'
# The folder deploy.sh publishes to and mcp_call.py runs the server from, as a Windows path
# (default: %LOCALAPPDATA%\mele-mcp\server).
# MELE_OUT='C:\mele-mcp'
# The server mcp_call.py runs, when it is not MELE_OUT's (default: MELE_OUT\MeleMcp.dll).
# MELE_DLL='C:\mele-mcp-test\MeleMcp.dll'
# mcp_call.py and mcp_smoke.py pass every other MELE_* setting on to the server, e.g. MELE_OWN_DLC (your mods' DLC
# folders, comma-separated, which catalog_index leaves out), MELE_LEVELS_JSON and MELE_BACKUP_DIR.
# MELE_OWN_DLC=DLC_MOD_MyMod
